            <ArticleTitle>The role of Th17 lymphocytes in the autoimmune and chronic inflammatory diseases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>487-95</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11739-011-0517-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The emerging role of interleukin-17 as a hallmark proinflammatory cytokine of the adaptive immune system produced by a new T helper cell subset termed &quot;Th17&quot; has received considerable attention. In this review we will focus on recent information regarding IL-17 and its relevance in autoimmune and chronic inflammatory diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
